        "1384027523": {
          "values": { "color": "var(--token-seU0DnRFH)" },
          "mixins": [],
          "__type": "RuleSet",
          "animations": null
        },
        "1384027524": {
          "markers": [],
          "text": "Internal tools are software applications used by an organization's team members to carry out their tasks more effectively. These may include project management tools, data analysis tools, communication platforms, and more.",
          "__type": "RawText"
        },
        "1384027525": {
          "values": { "padding-top": "0px" },
          "mixins": [],
          "__type": "RuleSet",
          "animations": null
        },
        "1384027526": {
          "markers": [],
          "text": "What types of internal tools can I build with Plasmic?",
          "__type": "RawText"
        },
        "1384027527": {
          "values": { "color": "var(--token-seU0DnRFH)" },
          "mixins": [],
          "__type": "RuleSet",
          "animations": null
        },
        "1384027528": {
          "markers": [],
          "text": "With Plasmic, you can build a wide range of internal tools, including project management tools, data analysis tools, dashboards, CRMs, and more. The platform's flexibility means it can be adapted to suit a vast array of use cases.",
          "__type": "RawText"
        },
        "1384027529": {
          "values": {},
          "mixins": [],
          "__type": "RuleSet",
          "animations": null
        },
        "1384027530": {
          "markers": [],
          "text": "How can I improve the user experience for my internal team members?",
          "__type": "RawText"
        },
        "1384027531": {
          "values": { "color": "var(--token-seU0DnRFH)" },
          "mixins": [],
          "__type": "RuleSet",
          "animations": null
        },
        "1384027532": {
          "markers": [],
          "text": "With Plasmic, you can leverage a set of building blocks that look and function great right out of the box. If you want to create a fully customized and unique user experience, Plasmic also allows you to tailor every element, from layout to functionality.",
          "__type": "RawText"
        },
        "1384027533": {
          "values": {},
          "mixins": [],
          "__type": "RuleSet",
          "animations": null
        },
        "1384027534": {
          "markers": [],
          "text": "Can non-technical team members use the internal tools built with Plasmic?",
          "__type": "RawText"
        },
        "1384027535": {
          "values": {
            "position": "relative",
            "color": "var(--token-seU0DnRFH)"
          },
          "mixins": [],
          "__type": "RuleSet",
          "animations": null
        },
        "1384027536": {
          "markers": [],
          "text": "Yes, Plasmic's internal tools are designed to be user-friendly. The tools you build can be made intuitive and straightforward, suitable for users with varying levels of technical expertise. Plus, with Plasmic's content creator mode, non-developers can safely make edits focusing just on content.",
          "__type": "RawText"
        },
        "1384027537": {
          "values": {},
          "mixins": [],
          "__type": "RuleSet",
          "animations": null
        },
        "1384027538": {
          "markers": [],
          "text": "How fast can I build an internal tool with Plasmic?",
          "__type": "RawText"
        },
        "1384027539": {
          "values": {
            "position": "relative",
            "color": "var(--token-seU0DnRFH)"
          },
          "mixins": [],
          "__type": "RuleSet",
          "animations": null
        },
        "1384027540": {
          "markers": [],
          "text": "Building internal tools with Plasmic can be much faster than traditional coding, thanks to its visual builder and pre-built components. The exact timeframe will depend on the complexity of the tool you're building, but the platform is designed to significantly speed up the development process.",
          "__type": "RawText"
        },
        "1384027541": {
          "values": {},
          "mixins": [],
          "__type": "RuleSet",
          "animations": null
        },
        "1384027542": {
          "markers": [],
          "text": "Can I integrate other software with the internal tools built on Plasmic?",
          "__type": "RawText"
        },
        "1384027543": {
          "values": {
            "position": "relative",
            "color": "var(--token-seU0DnRFH)"
          },
          "mixins": [],
          "__type": "RuleSet",
          "animations": null
        },
        "1384027544": {
          "markers": [],
          "text": "Yes, Plasmic allows for integrations with various other software. This means you can pull in data from or push data to other platforms your team is already using, which can greatly enhance the effectiveness of your internal tools.",
          "__type": "RawText"
        },
        "1384027545": {
          "values": {},
          "mixins": [],
          "__type": "RuleSet",
          "animations": null
        },
        "1384027546": {
          "markers": [],
          "text": "Is it possible to scale internal tools as my business grows?",
          "__type": "RawText"
        },
        "1384027547": {
          "values": {
            "position": "relative",
            "color": "var(--token-seU0DnRFH)"
          },
          "mixins": [],
          "__type": "RuleSet",
          "animations": null
        },
        "1384027548": {
          "markers": [],
          "text": "Absolutely. With Plasmic, scalability is built in. The platform is designed to grow with your business, allowing you to add more data sources, custom components, and integrations as needed. Furthermore, deploying your tools as a React application or integrating with your existing infrastructure ensures that you maintain full control over the tool's environment, facilitating easy scaling as your team expands.",
          "__type": "RawText"
        },
